{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511843-mi-as-the-arabic-word-for-quicksand-the-political-system-of-the-order-of-hermes","id":1511843,"title":"Mi'as: The Arabic word for 'quicksand' & the political system of the Order of Hermes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-17T00:42:13-07:00","id":1511843,"title":"Mi'as: The Arabic word for 'quicksand' & the political system of the Order of Hermes","content":"Is it really a word? <br /> <br /> The book says it is (this can be found on page 43 of OoH revised).<br /> <br /> I have been looking and found no evidence of this.<br /> <br /> I have been trying to find some reference to the use of &quot;Mi'as&quot; in Arabic and have found none (for quicksand or any other meaning). <br /> <br /> Can anyone help throw some light on this matter???<br /> <br /> Did they just make it up??? \ud83d\ude02 <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T03:42:48-07:00","id":1511851,"title":"","content":"There's always the possibility that someone botched their Language roll. Also, we are talking Order of Hermes. Mi'as could be an obscure classical literary term. Formal Arabic literary and poetic diction is supposed to be much further from spoken Arabic than such things are in English. Think about some of the odder and now out of fashion quirks of English language poetry. Remember Milton's &quot;Star ypointing pyramid.&quot; The y was slapped in for the sake of the meter. The use of 'ere' for before still occurs in the 20th century (I know of no use of ere in 21st century poetry). English, had many such &quot;poetic forms&quot; long out of fashion, only Faerie and Eldritch get much use. Arabic always had a far more developed poetic diction than English ever did. Though the numbers of truly great poets are comparable given factors of population and market.<br /> <br /> Mi'as could simply be obscure and literary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-18-2023, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T06:21:01-07:00","id":1512006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511843-mi-as-the-arabic-word-for-quicksand-the-political-system-of-the-order-of-hermes#post1511843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it really a word?<br /> <br /> The book says it is (this can be found on page 43 of OoH revised).<br /> <br /> I have been looking and found no evidence of this.<br /> <br /> I have been trying to find some reference to the use of &quot;Mi'as&quot; in Arabic and have found none (for quicksand or any other meaning).<br /> <br /> Can anyone help throw some light on this matter???<br /> <br /> Did they just make it up??? \ud83d\ude02<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One lead to working out this matter / issue is checking whether Mages from the Order of Hermes use this term, phrase, or word in a mundane way ( independently of language they are using in a particular situation ) while speaking, discussing, writing paper letters and correspondence, or scirbing books and literature. <br /> <br /> This word could be used in this context and with that meaning by some relatively mnior or small organisations and groups - because of this it might be difficult to sings, proof, indications, and evidence that this term, word, or phrase is regularly and normally used and known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T15:17:20-07:00","id":1512387,"title":"","content":"Google says it's a Spanish-word, so, there's a possibility it's an obscure Moorish word but the meaning is, &quot;My Ace&quot;. &quot;Mi&quot;, in Arabic comes up as Music or Religion. The author's failed their Mind-Sphere roll to coincidentally make the word an Arabic-word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T15:55:59-07:00","id":1512921,"title":"","content":"Plugging \u201cquicksand\u201d into Google Translate tells me that the Arabic term is \u201calrimal almutaharika\u201d. So I really hope there is another term for quicksand - perhaps localised to any Arabic-speaking regions that actually have quicksand - because by the time somebody says \u201caihtaris min tilk alrimal almutaharika\u201d (\u201cWatch out for that quicksand\u201d) somebody else has surely sunk beneath it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}